Project Title

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on Retail Sales Data

Objective

The objective of this project is to perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on retail sales data to identify sales trends, customer purchasing behavior, and product performance. The analysis helps businesses make informed decisions using data-driven insights.

Dataset

The dataset contains retail sales transaction information including:

Customer details
Product information
Sales amount
Quantity purchased
Order dates
Tools and Libraries Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Jupyter Notebook
Steps Performed
1. Data Loading
Imported the retail sales dataset using Pandas.
2. Data Cleaning
Checked missing values
Removed duplicates
Converted date columns into datetime format
3. Descriptive Statistics

Calculated:

Mean
Median
Mode
Standard Deviation
4. Time Series Analysis
Analyzed monthly sales trends
Identified high and low sales periods
5. Customer and Product Analysis
Analyzed customer purchasing behavior
Identified top-selling products/categories
6. Data Visualization

Created:

Bar Charts
Line Plots
Heatmaps
7. Recommendations

Provided business recommendations based on sales trends and customer behavior.

Key Insights
Certain months showed significantly higher sales.
Some product categories generated more revenue than others.
Customer purchasing patterns helped identify popular products.
Outcome

This project improved understanding of:

Data cleaning techniques
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
Time series analysis
Data visualization
Business insight generation
Conclusion

The project successfully analyzed retail sales data and generated meaningful insights that can help improve business strategies and customer satisfaction.